// KNOWN SILENT-WRONG (open) — the generic-over-wide representation keystone.
// NOT gated: this file documents a bug the medium does not yet catch. It
// compiles clean (zero diagnostics) and runs to the WRONG answer.
//
// `sum` threads an UNANNOTATED accumulator `acc`. Inference leaves `acc` a
// type variable (the list element is a free var when `sum` is checked), so the
// function compiles ONCE at the RI32 floor: `(param $acc i32)`, `(i32.add)`.
// main then calls it with a native-f64 [Float] list — the f64 values cross into
// the i32-compiled body and are read as words. The sum is garbage (~0), and
// nothing refuses: exit 1 (the `else`), never 42.
//
// This is the SCALAR half of band D's `Hβ.value.seq-element-stride-carrier`,
// which names TWO solutions: a runtime stride carrier OR whole-program
// monomorphization. The stride carrier SHIPPED (7db29195) and fixed the
// SEQUENCE-READ half — `list_index(xs, i)` reads the element stride live, so a
// generic body reading a packed [Float]/[Byte] is sound (proven here: annotate
// `acc: Float` and the SAME sequence read runs 42). What is left open is the
// MONOMORPHIZATION half: `acc` is a scalar generic over the numeric type
// (`sum : ([a], Int, a) -> a`, a = Int or Float via `+`), and the fn compiles
// ONCE at the i32 floor, so a Float call reads the doubles as words. The
// stride carrier does not touch scalar params; only monomorphization (specialize
// the fn at the repr its call demands) makes this run 42 without the annotation.
// A refusal-at-the-mismatch would be a STOPGAP monomorphization deletes, so the
// ultimate is monomorphization itself. Annotating `acc: Float` is manual
// monomorphization and is what CFC + tests/frontier/mn-float-*.mn use today.
//
// SCOPE (measured, against an earlier overstatement): the whole prelude
// combinator surface — fold / reduce / map / filter / each — handles floats
// CORRECTLY, because their accumulators are lambdas or handler state, specialized
// per call site with the concrete type. The floor bites ONLY a NAMED top-level
// recursive fn with an unannotated wide param, compiled once. So this is a
// corner, not a pervasive hole; most float code (combinators, annotated helpers)
// is sound today.
//
// Surfaced 2026-07-21 by representation-stress probing while migrating the CFC
// pipeline to native [Float]. Turn this into a frontier gate (expecting 42, or
// a run_refusal) when the keystone lands.
fn sum(xs, i, acc) with Memory =
  if i >= 3 { acc } else { sum(xs, i + 1, acc + list_index(xs, i)) }

fn main() = {
  let xs = [0.5, 1.5, 2.5]           // native [Float], sums to 4.5
  if sum(xs, 0, 0.0) == 4.5 { 42 } else { 1 }
}
